Negative control for the detail action bar EXCLUDING its opener (FE-3091
operator refinement 1).

Restores the whole row-action set to the read overlay, so the `detail`/view
verb that OPENED the overlay is offered again inside it — the very thing the
refinement removed, mirroring how the editor never re-offers Edit.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the detail-action-bar spec — opening a record on its `view` (`detail`)
control must leave that control OUT of the overlay's own action bar while every
OTHER row action (Edit, etc.) still rides there.

